  1309	
  1310	/**Function*************************************************************
  1311	
  1312	  Synopsis    [Returns 1 if a fanout/load proxy should reject this cut.]
  1313	
  1314	  Description [Mode 1 is the classic map -f guard. Mode 2 is the stmap1
  1315	  selective guard, which only rejects wider cuts when the node has higher
  1316	  estimated fanout. Mode 3 is the stmap2 guard, which uses the same fanout
  1317	  thresholds only during area recovery and only when the current phase has
  1318	  slack over the mapper required time. Mode 4 is the stmap3 guard, which
  1319	  narrows the intervention to high-fanout nodes with only shallow positive
  1320	  slack. Mode 5 is the stmap4 split-phase guard: stmap1-style guarding in
  1321	  delay matching and stmap2-style slack-aware guarding in area recovery.
  1322	  Mode 6 is the stmap5 shape-gated split-phase guard: the delay pass only
  1323	  uses stmap1-style guarding in very large mapper graphs, while area recovery
  1324	  keeps the stmap2 slack-aware guard. Mode 7 is the stmap6 area-sensitive
  1325	  shape-gated guard: the delay pass keeps the stmap5 graph-size gate, small
  1326	  mapper graphs keep the stmap2 slack-aware recovery guard, and exact-area
  1327	  recovery on larger graphs checks the cut after matching so materially cheaper
  1328	  cuts can override the fanout/load proxy. Mode 8 is the stmap7 criticality-
  1329	  sensitive version of mode 7: exact-area recovery on larger graphs allows the
  1330	  override only with deeper mapper slack and outside the highest fanout bucket.
  1331	  Mode 9 is the stmap8 arrival-bounded version of mode 8: the area-saving
  1332	  override also requires the candidate match to stay within one quarter of an
  1333	  inverter delay of the existing mapper arrival. Mode 10 is the stmap9
  1334	  middle-slack area-relief version of mode 9: it keeps the highest fanout
  1335	  bucket protected, but in the one-to-two inverter slack bucket it allows a
  1336	  wide cut only when it is arrival-neutral and saves at least one inverter
  1337	  area. Mode 11 is the stmap10 depth-qualified version of mode 10: the
  1338	  middle-slack relief is allowed only for shallow and medium-depth nodes.
  1339	  Mode 12 is the stmap11 tight-depth version of mode 11: the middle-slack
  1340	  relief is allowed only for shallower nodes. Mode 13 is the stmap12
  1341	  fanout-bucket split version of mode 12: the tight-depth middle-slack relief
  1342	  is allowed only in the lower moderate fanout bucket. Mode 14 is stmap13,
  1343	  which keeps mode 13 behavior while recording guard-hit counters. Mode 15 is
  1344	  stmap14, which keeps the same bucket and counters but requires a stronger
  1345	  middle-slack area-flow saving. Mode 16 is stmap15, which restores the
  1346	  one-inverter relief threshold only after the current run has observed a high
  1347	  lower-moderate/middle-slack exact-area profile. Mode 17 is stmap16, which
  1348	  keeps mode 16 behavior and prints per-relief diagnostics. Mode 18 is stmap17,
  1349	  which uses the one-inverter post-profile threshold only for candidates with
  1350	  materially better mapper arrival. Mode 19 is stmap18, which keeps mode 18
  1351	  decisions and adds near-miss diagnostics for candidates rejected by the
  1352	  timing-quality/profile fallback. Mode 20 is stmap19, which allows the
  1353	  one-inverter threshold before profile-open only for candidates with the same
  1354	  material mapper-arrival improvement. Mode 21 is stmap20, which keeps the
  1355	  mode 20 pre-profile seed but restricts it to shallow nodes. Mode 22 is
  1356	  stmap21, which keeps the shallow seed and admits deeper pre-profile seeds
  1357	  only when the arrival gain is unusually large. Mode 23 is stmap22, which
  1358	  relaxes the deep pre-profile seed boundary to a moderate arrival gain. Mode
  1359	  24 is stmap23, which keeps the strong deep seeds but allows moderate deep
  1360	  seeds only when the existing mapper slack is near the critical side of the
  1361	  middle-slack window. Mode 25 is stmap24, which tightens the moderate deep
  1362	  slack gate to the lower edge of that critical window. Mode 26 is stmap25,
  1363	  which keeps stmap24 and admits at most one moderate deep seed from the next
  1364	  slack band as an ablation diagnostic. Mode 27 is stmap26, which skips the
  1365	  first such moderate seed and admits only the second qualifying seed. Mode 28
  1366	  is stmap27, which reopens the next slack band except for the high-reference,
  1367	  low-slack, stronger-moderate signature isolated by stmap26. Mode 29 is
  1368	  stmap28, which replaces that hard signature blocker with a high-reference
  1369	  moderate-seed area penalty that scales with reference count, slack risk, and
  1370	  arrival-gain risk. Mode 30 is stmap29, which keeps the same seed band but
  1371	  makes the penalty a continuous load-risk gradient. Mode 31 is stmap30,
  1372	  which keeps that moderate-seed gradient and adds a smaller continuous
  1373	  penalty to high-reference strong deep seeds. Mode 32 is stmap31, which keeps
  1374	  mode 31's moderate penalty but dampens the strong-seed gain slope. Mode 33
  1375	  is stmap32, which adds a cut-leaf load proxy to the strong-seed penalty. Mode
  1376	  34 is stmap33, which normalizes that load proxy by supergate fanout limit.
  1377	  Mode 35 is stmap34, which uses a bounded sublinear load/drive curve. Mode
  1378	  36 is stmap35, which preserves that mapper curve while command-level SCL
  1379	  load/max-cap diagnostics are emitted. Mode 37 is stmap36, which strengthens
  1380	  the bounded curve according to direct SCL over-cap severity measured by a
  1381	  command-layer first pass. Mode 38 is stmap37, which applies that feedback
  1382	  only when the current mapper node appears in the first-pass over-cap
  1383	  hotspot set. Mode 39 is stmap38, which broadens the local association to
  1384	  command-collected fanout users and candidate cut leaves. Mode 40 is stmap39,
  1385	  which replaces the static hotspot neighborhood with command-collected
  1386	  downstream consumer pressure. Mode 41 is stmap40, which preserves those
  1387	  pressure ratios in a dense AIG-ID lookup so medium-pressure reconstruction
  1388	  IDs are not discarded by a capped table. Mode 42 is stmap41, which uses the
  1389	  same dense transfer but weights pressure by first-pass SCL timing criticality
  1390	  before it can increase the strong-seed area margin. Mode 43 is stmap42, which
  1391	  propagates sink criticality from over-cap consumers into their fanin pressure
  1392	  cones with a bounded raw-pressure floor. Mode 44 is stmap43, which keeps the
  1393	  sink-pressure strong-seed protection but gates moderate deep area penalties
  1394	  by the same sink-pressure vector so unpressured paths can recover area.]
  1395	
  1396	  SideEffects []
  1397	
  1398	  SeeAlso     []
