  1563	/**Function*************************************************************
  1564	
  1565	  Synopsis    [Returns 1 if an stmap area-sensitive mode should reject a cut.]
  1566	
  1567	  Description [The area-sensitive guards are evaluated after matching the
  1568	  candidate cut because their hypotheses need the candidate's actual mapper
  1569	  area. In stmap6 exact-area recovery, a wide high-fanout cut is rejected only
  1570	  when the existing match has slack and the candidate does not save at least
  1571	  half an inverter area. In stmap7, the area-saving override additionally
  1572	  requires more than two inverter delays of slack and excludes the highest
  1573	  fanout-risk bucket. In stmap8, the override is further rejected when the
  1574	  candidate match worsens mapper arrival by more than one quarter of an
  1575	  inverter delay. In stmap9, middle-slack candidates can recover area only
  1576	  when they are outside the highest fanout bucket, do not worsen mapper
  1577	  arrival, and save at least one inverter area. In stmap10, that middle-slack
  1578	  relief also requires the mapper node to be no deeper than level 96. In
  1579	  stmap11, that depth window is tightened to level 64. In stmap12, the same
  1580	  tight-depth relief is allowed only in the lower moderate fanout bucket. In
  1581	  stmap13, the same decision path also records exact-area guard statistics. In
  1582	  stmap14, the lower-moderate middle-slack relief must save two inverter areas
  1583	  instead of one. In stmap15, one-inverter relief is restored only after the
  1584	  mapper observes a high lower-moderate/middle-slack profile. In stmap16, the
  1585	  same behavior also reports each admitted relief choice. In stmap17, the
  1586	  adaptive one-inverter relief threshold also requires a material mapper-arrival
  1587	  improvement; arrival-neutral choices keep the stricter two-inverter fallback.
  1588	  In stmap18, the same decisions are preserved while near-miss rejected
  1589	  middle-slack candidates are logged. In stmap19, pre-profile one-inverter
  1590	  relief is seeded only by candidates with the same material arrival gain. In
  1591	  stmap20, the pre-profile seed is further limited to shallow nodes. In
  1592	  stmap21, deeper pre-profile seeds are allowed only with a much larger mapper
  1593	  arrival gain. In stmap22, the same deep-seed path is relaxed to a moderate
  1594	  mapper-arrival gain. In stmap23, moderate deep seeds also need near-critical
  1595	  existing mapper slack. In stmap24, the moderate deep slack gate is tightened
  1596	  to the lower edge of the critical slack window. In stmap25, the stmap24 rule
  1597	  is kept, and one moderate deep seed from the next slack band is admitted for
  1598	  ablation. In stmap26, the first such moderate seed is skipped and only the
  1599	  second qualifying seed is admitted. In stmap27, moderate deep candidates in
  1600	  the next slack band are admitted unless they match the high-reference,
  1601	  low-slack, stronger-moderate signature isolated by stmap26. In stmap28, that
  1602	  hard blocker is replaced by a soft area-margin penalty on high-reference
  1603	  moderate seeds whose slack and arrival-gain ratios resemble load-risky
  1604	  choices. In stmap29, the high-reference penalty is made continuous over the
  1605	  same seed band. In stmap30, the same load-risk surface is extended to
  1606	  high-reference strong deep seeds with a smaller continuous penalty. In
  1607	  stmap31, the strong-seed gain slope is damped to probe the penalty threshold.
  1608	  In stmap32, a cut-leaf load proxy adds a candidate-cut fanout-shape term to
  1609	  the strong-seed penalty. In stmap33, the cut-leaf term is normalized by the
  1610	  selected supergate fanout limit to test a library-derived drive/load signal.
  1611	  In stmap34, the drive-normalized term uses a bounded sublinear curve so high
  1612	  load/drive ratios do not automatically saturate the area margin. Stmap35
  1613	  preserves the stmap34 mapper decision surface and adds direct SCL
  1614	  mapped-load diagnostics in the command layer. Stmap36 feeds the aggregate
  1615	  direct SCL load/max-cap severity from a first pass back into the same bounded
  1616	  strong-seed area margin. Stmap37 restricts that SCL feedback to first-pass
  1617	  over-cap hotspot AIG IDs and their immediate mapped fanin cone. Stmap38
  1618	  broadens the first-pass association and checks candidate cut leaves against
  1619	  that hotspot set before applying the local SCL feedback term. Stmap39 carries
  1620	  first-pass SCL load pressure onto downstream consumers and their fanin cones,
  1621	  then lets strong-seed candidates use the maximum node/cut consumer pressure
  1622	  as the local SCL feedback term. Stmap40 keeps the same pressure source but
  1623	  passes it as a dense AIG-ID vector so medium-pressure reconstructed IDs survive
  1624	  the command-to-mapper boundary. Stmap41 keeps dense pressure but gates its
  1625	  strength by first-pass SCL criticality, reducing non-critical over-cap hits
  1626	  before they affect mapper area recovery. Stmap42 instead propagates the
  1627	  over-cap consumer's criticality into the fanin cone and keeps a bounded
  1628	  raw-pressure floor for sink-correlated load pressure. Stmap43 keeps the
  1629	  strong-seed sink-pressure rule but applies moderate deep penalties only when
  1630	  the candidate or its leaves have material sink-pressure, letting unpressured
  1631	  area-recovery candidates use the lighter one-inverter margin.]
  1632	
  1633	  SideEffects []
  1634	
  1635	  SeeAlso     []
  1636	
  1637	***********************************************************************/
